sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-competency-06> a delphi:Claim ;
    rdfs:label "Competent embryos take over mixed populations given enough competency or numbers" ;
    dct:description "In mixed populations of the 1D artificial embryogeny model, competent embryos starting as a minority came to dominate hardwired ones within two or three generations, and the competency needed to dominate fell as their initial share rose (75 at 10%, 40 at 20%, 10 at 30%), while at 2.5% they did not dominate even at competency 95." ;
    delphi:context "Shreesha L, Levin M, “Cellular Competency during Development Alters Evolutionary Dynamics in an Artificial Embryogeny Model”, Entropy (Basel, Switzerland) (2023), doi:10.3390/e25010131; section “3. Results › 3.3. Competent Individuals Take over Mixed Populations”. Scope: In silico mixed populations of 200 hardwired and competent 1D embryos" ;
    dct:type "simulation-result" .
}

